## Installation

### Marketplace or HACS

[![Open your Home Assistant instance and open this repository in HACS.](https://my.home-assistant.io/badges/hacs_repository.svg)](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/hacs_repository/?owner=jasonaward&repository={{ repo }}&category=integration)

[![Open your Home Assistant instance and start setting up this integration.](https://my.home-assistant.io/badges/config_flow_start.svg)](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/config_flow_start/?domain={{ domain }})

The first button opens this repository in the Marketplace or HACS, whichever you have.
Without the buttons, on Home Assistant 2026.11 and later:

1. Go to **Settings** > **Marketplace** and select **Add from link**.
2. In **GitHub link**, enter `https://github.com/jasonaward/{{ repo }}` and select
   **Add**. Adding a repository that isn't in the Marketplace's catalog asks you to
   connect a GitHub account first.
3. Open **{{ name }}** and install it.
4. Follow [Configuration](#configuration). Updates need a restart; the first install
   doesn't.

On earlier versions, with HACS:

1. In HACS, select the three dots menu > **Custom repositories**.
2. Add `https://github.com/jasonaward/{{ repo }}` with the type **Integration**.
3. Find **{{ name }}** and select **Download**.
4. Restart Home Assistant, then follow [Configuration](#configuration).

**Betas.** While this integration is in beta, every release is a pre-release, which you
only get once you've asked for them:

- **Marketplace**: on this repository's page, select the three dots menu > **Install
  another version** and choose the beta. To get later betas as updates, turn on
  pre-releases for the repository: **Include pre-releases** in the same menu or, on some
  versions, the repository device's **Pre-release** switch.
- **HACS**: turn on the repository's pre-release switch (an entity of its device in HACS,
  disabled by default).

### Manual

1. Download `{{ domain }}.zip` from the
   [latest release](https://github.com/jasonaward/{{ repo }}/releases).
2. Unzip it into `config/custom_components/{{ domain }}/`.
3. Restart Home Assistant, then follow [Configuration](#configuration).

